2186123050 1078 #edb/ref 17592186447333 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124454 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447370 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124454 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447373 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124455 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447372 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124456 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447371 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124456 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447374 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124732 1050 840.0 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124979 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124979 1071 "Given the function $f(x, y) = 3x^{2} + 2xy^{2} - y$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x, y) = (-1, 1)$." 13194139534998 17592186045417 false] [17592186124979 1071 "Given the function $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(-1,1).$" 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186124979 1074 "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y)\\,j \\\\  & =(6x+2{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+(4xy-1)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,1) & =(6(-1)+2(1)^{2})\\,i+(4(-1)(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =-4\\,i-5\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-4,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-4,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186125075 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186125075 1071 "Given the function $f(x, y) = \\cos (x^{2}) - 3y^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x, y) = (\\sqrt{π}, 2)$." 13194139534998 17592186045417 false] [17592186125075 1071 "Given the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(\\sqrt{\\pi },2).$" 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186125075 1074 "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(\\sqrt{\\pi },2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3})\\,j \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})\\,i-9{y}^{2}\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(\\sqrt{\\pi },2) & =-2\\sqrt{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡((\\sqrt{\\pi })^{2})i-9(2)^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot 0\\,i-36\\,j \\\\  & =-36\\,j \\\\  & =⟨0,-36⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\sqrt{\\pi },2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186447330 1080 "⟨11,-10⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186447330 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [17592186447330 1083 #uuid "16af8390-5001-553a-b0f4-0d97c561270f" 13194139534998 17592186045417 true] [175921864473